{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FHXNwqZvycCfV28p2NQ9tG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review review form 2025 2026 soundness excitement overall assessment score scale 1-5\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2026 on X: \\\"Checkout the blog post on the soundness/excitement scores https://t.co/AKSO9DjiYP . It clarifies the reasoning behind the separation of overall scores and how it might make the reviewer recommendation more robust. #ACL2023Toronto #ACL2023NLP #NLProc\\\" / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/aclmeeting/status/1637827267173953540\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about the ACL Rolling Review form for 2025-2026:\n\n## Review Scoring Structure\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness Score\n\nThe soundness assessment considers whether the paper is sufficiently sound and thorough, whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them, and for experimental papers examines the depth and/or breadth of research questions investigated, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation.\n\nThe soundness score uses a 1-5 scale:\n- 5 = Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type.\n- 4 = Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims. Some extra experiments could be nice, but not essential.\n- 3 = Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims.\n\n### Excitement Score\n\nExcitement is subjective and does not necessarily follow what is popular in the field. The excitement score also uses a 1-5 scale:\n- 5 = Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference.\n- 4 = Exciting: I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation in a conference.\n- 1 = Not Exciting: this paper does not resonate with me, and I don't think it would with others in the *ACL community (e.g. it is in no way related to computational processing of language).\n\n### Overall Assessment Score\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3aaeb28d-6087-4473-966f-cc5fed7a013d","uuid":"cadc1e03-c1be-481e-a904-de8f43cfb5fc","timestamp":"2026-05-17T08:43:58.645Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review review form 2025 2026 soundness excitement overall assessment score scale 1-5","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01PYaW4LiFErpd64rzVUAcbF","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md"},{"title":"ACL 2026 on X: \"Checkout the blog post on the soundness/excitement scores https://t.co/AKSO9DjiYP . It clarifies the reasoning behind the separation of overall scores and how it might make the reviewer recommendation more robust. #ACL2023Toronto #ACL2023NLP #NLProc\" / X","url":"https://x.com/aclmeeting/status/1637827267173953540"},{"title":"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \"Publish or Perish\" Circus | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"}]},"Based on the search results, here's information about the ACL Rolling Review form for 2025-2026:\n\n## Review Scoring Structure\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness Score\n\nThe soundness assessment considers whether the paper is sufficiently sound and thorough, whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them, and for experimental papers examines the depth and/or breadth of research questions investigated, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation.\n\nThe soundness score uses a 1-5 scale:\n- 5 = Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type.\n- 4 = Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims. Some extra experiments could be nice, but not essential.\n- 3 = Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims.\n\n### Excitement Score\n\nExcitement is subjective and does not necessarily follow what is popular in the field. The excitement score also uses a 1-5 scale:\n- 5 = Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference.\n- 4 = Exciting: I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation in a conference.\n- 1 = Not Exciting: this paper does not resonate with me, and I don't think it would with others in the *ACL community (e.g. it is in no way related to computational processing of language).\n\n### Overall Assessment Score\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact."],"durationSeconds":8.061488700999998}}
